\begin{theorem}[Recent chains share their deep blocks; Lean
\code{timed\_light\_client\_safety}]\label{thm:lc}
Fix $n \ge 1$ and a deployment genesis $G$. Suppose:
\begin{itemize}
\item a timed execution (\code{TimedExecution}): signing happens at real slots;
  at a bad real slot the producer's key signs arbitrarily many blocks with
  any stamp in its residue class (\code{key\_match}); an honest real slot
  signs only its own current block (\code{honest\_stamp}) and at most once
  (\code{honest\_once}); a block is signed only once its parent is available
  (\code{chain\_order}); and collision resistance holds over occurring blocks
  (\code{id\_inj});
\item the fault budget over real slots: $\code{ByzantineBounded}\ n\ \mathit{bad}$;
\item the verifier is at real slot $R$, and every producer signature it accepts
  was produced at some real slot no later than $R$ (\code{hbridge}: EUF-CMA
  plus causality);
\item there are two presentations, each consisting of a grounded certificate
  claim (\code{GroundedCert}) and a suffix that passes the validator:
  linkage to the claim (\code{hLink}), internal linkage (\code{hLinks}),
  density of maturing windows (\code{hDense}), and verifying signatures
  (\code{hSigned});
\item both tips are recent in real time: $R \le \mathit{tip.slot} + n$.
\end{itemize}
Then, taking any histories the two groundings attest (\code{GroundedHistory}),
the two full chains (attested history concatenated with suffix) agree at
every height $h$ with $h + n$ below both full lengths. Equivalently, they
agree on everything at least $n$ blocks below the lower tip.
\end{theorem}

